+# TB-SEC-KEY-01-R2A-R1 — local authenticated account handoff
+
+Status: implementation candidate, partial acceptance. No real credentials, provider calls or live authorization.
+
+## Implementation
+
+Settings retains status-only account connections for installed mode. The opt-in local handoff is the fixed `majvaj-account:open` intent, without a bearer, credential, caller-selected target, or trading authorization. Clicking the handoff clears the browser's authenticated application state; page departure and persisted-page restoration also clear that state. A dedicated, independently authenticated `maj-vaj-console` Linux desktop is designed to start a local browser with a temporary private profile. The handler requires the console principal, separated groups, an explicit root-owned activation marker, the same active local seat and caller session, and a stable private display identity. It requires explicit local confirmation to end only its own session; entry to the existing independent credential-operator desktop requires fresh OS authentication. Cancellation, changed identity and lock events refuse the transition. Local manual sign-out remains the fallback; a remote browser does not gain a local launch or enrollment capability. The native browser and desktop provisioning require administrator review and cannot create credentials or enable trading. The original development test-only form remains distinct.
+
+## Executed qualification
+
+- Restored R2A source candidate and retained locked React 18.3.1 dependencies unchanged.
+- Nine focused handoff tests passed. Full Python suite: 543 discovered, 541 passed, two optional skips, exit 0. Node render/source check and Python/shell syntax checks passed.
+- Offline QEMU child of the previously qualified Debian desktop: nine changed runtime/deployment files were hashed; provision preflight refused missing Chromium and xdg-utils, as expected. Desk, credential operator, dashboard-auth and a console principal with no active local session were refused. A test-only LightDM fixture reached an authenticated console seat, following initial greeter authentication/session-selection retries; positive native confirmation and session retirement were NOT verified. Fixture teardown completed; child disk check passed and all three backing image hashes remained unchanged.
+- The shared npm cache contained React 19, not the exact React 18.3.1 lock. Offline locked install failed. Host browser smoke attempted with separate compatibility fixture assets, not a replacement lockfile or production build; Chromium returned ERR_BLOCKED_BY_ADMINISTRATOR on initial navigation. No browser security or persistence result is claimed; no restriction was bypassed. Prepared synthetic browser test remains unexecuted beyond initial navigation. Browser-to-desktop URI dispatch, browser lifecycle and no-persistence checks, actual confirmation/cancellation and fresh credential operator login after handoff require qualification on an authorized installed desktop with the exact assets and supported browser.
+
+## Remaining gates
+
+Obtain/restore the exact locked dashboard npm packages and a supported offline browser/xdg package set (or an authorized equivalent deployment environment), then execute installed positive and negative handoff, browser persistence, independent identity and post-handoff graphical enrollment checks. This is local console handoff, not remote HTTPS account enrollment. R2B provider permission checks/pairing, R2C security and recovery, and separate PAPER/forward-validation release gates remain open. Do not enter real credentials.
